Package: HDMaxShrink
Type: Package
Title: Test-Guided Shrinkage for High-Dimensional Linear Models
Version: 0.6.2
Authors@R: 
    person("Bahadir", "Yuzbasi", email = "b.yzb@hotmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre"))
Author: Bahadir Yuzbasi [aut, cre]
Maintainer: Bahadir Yuzbasi <b.yzb@hotmail.com>
Description: Fits test-guided shrinkage estimators in sparse linear models
    where the number of predictors may exceed the sample size. Version 0.6.2
    preserves the version 0.6.1 statistical API and implements the optional
    CPSS--MCP sensitivity path with singleton-group MCP from 'grpreg', using
    the same documented relative lower penalty bound as CPSS--LASSO. Version
    0.6.1 added portable
    LAPACK/BLAS/Fortran linkage for the compiled RcppArmadillo kernels.
    Version 0.6.0 added mandatory-core conditional complementary-pairs stability selection,
    an exact-null low-dimensional SVD submodel refit, and an
    all-predictor dual-Ridge full endpoint. Their difference is combined by a
    conditional Gaussian maximum partial-t test to form preliminary-test,
    Stein-type, positive-part, and pretest-protected positive-part estimators.
    The earlier joint all-predictor square-root-LASSO framework remains
    available. Within each fit,
    predictor columns and the response are centered and root-mean-square
    scaled, the standardized intercept is fixed at zero, and returned
    coefficients are on the original scale. A conditional Gaussian maximum
    partial-t test and an inverse-null-moment calibration define the
    interpolation weights. Economy SVD and compiled
    RcppArmadillo kernels avoid ordinary-least-squares Gram inverses, q by q
    covariance inverses, and p by p inverses. Earlier partial, Ridge--MCP, and
    restriction-projection frameworks remain available as sensitivity and
    reproducibility modes.
